nd Strange  World Meridian is a strong supporting  character acting as a rock for both  husband Searcher and Son Ethan and she  even gets to save them from time to time  but her character and specifically her  name has a deeper meaning that  reinforces her role in the movie  [Music]  Meridian is not necessarily a common  name but it is an intentional choice  that makes sense for the character Avid  geographers will know that Meridian is  an astronomical and geographical term  used by explorers and adventurers which  refers to a line of longitude the prime  meridian for instance is a center line  where longitude is zero degrees in the  movie Meridian assertion Center as she  grounds him additionally while he lives  his life as a farmer there is a small  reluctant part of Searcher that wants to  be an Explorer the fact that his wife's  name is a geographical term is seemingly  another clue that he subconsciously  Longs for adventure  the biggest scene that runs throughout  strange world is the intergenerational  conflict between Fathers and Sons both  Diego and serger and serger and Ethan  have their own issues communicating and  connecting with one another in fact  searcher's relationship with his son is  informed by how his father treated him  which touches on the theme of  generational trauma however Strange  World also has a sense of how  male-centric the story might seem and it  Endeavors to prioritize its female  characters Jaeger Sergio and Ethan find  themselves running from some angry  wildlife and they find themselves  scrambling through the Flora and Fauna  luckily Meridian and president Mal show  up just in time to rescue them from  turning into alien food in this moment  the women of strange world have an  opportunity to shine is this thing  dangerous  in Strange World Alan tudek voices  secutes and gelatinous splat the blue  blob is one of two playful companions in  the movie The Other being the clade's  adorable three-legged Pooch Legend  Disney regularly includes cute and  cuddly companions in his animated movies  and at younger audiences and strange  world even acknowledges and pokes fun at  this practice at one point in the movie  a member of the crew noticed a Splat for  the first time and freaks out getting  very excited even points to Splat and  says it's so cute I want to merchandise  it this joke might go over the heads of  the film's younger audience but Disney's  practice of creating cute characters in  order to sell toys is well documented in  everything from Strange World to Star  Wars in Strange World each of the three  clayed men take Journeys to find  acceptance and peace with their family  in a multi-layered hero's journey the  movie focuses most on Ethan the youngest  character and the most relatable to a  young diverse audience Ethan struggles  with breaking out of the bugs that his  father is forcing him into and refuge  users to accept a future as a farmer  instead Ethan longs to be an Explorer  like his long-loster grandfather so when  the two finally meet at long last and  get to know each other they hit it off  extremely well a strange World continues  it becomes clear that Ethan resembles  his grandfather and naturally takes on  some of his mannerisms there's even a  moment on the airstrip during which  Ethan and Jaeger stand next to one  another and they hold themselves in the  exact same pose with their hands on  their hips front foot outward and ready  to Take On The World the pose itself  emphasizes The Adventurous spirit that  the two share it is a quick moment and  its significance is easy to miss but  this theme is reinforced throughout the  movie as Ethan takes after several other  characters as well Jaeger isn't the only  Fundy member Ethan has inherited traits  and mannerisms from drawing Strange  World it becomes clear that Ethan's  mother Meridian has also inspired many  of her son's traits from their need for  conversation to the way they stand Ethan  and Meridian share many similarities  Ethan shared traits with his mother and  grandfather only highlights how much  distance Ethan feels from his dad  Searcher for instance throughout the  movie Ethan goes to everyone for help  except for his dad on the surface Ethan  seems to be more like Jaeger and  Meridian than his own father and search  here is painfully aware of this fact and  becomes hopelessly fixated on it but  it's not until the final act that both  Father and Son realize what they truly  have in common I'm not my father  meanwhile search's relationship with his  own father is challenging plus that  rocky relationship didn't get any better  when Jaeger abandoned him and took off  without warning it takes most of the  movie for them to reconcile but serger  and his father eventually start to set  aside their differences and warm up to  one another they eventually spend some  time hanging out together and start to  bond after the longest time apart the  difficulties they face will be relatable  to anyone who has ever fallen out with a  family member or long to bond with a  distant parent or relative  at the start of the movie Ethan's Crush  stops by and drops off a new card for a  game called Primal Outpost at first it  looks as though Primal outposts may  share some similarities with magic the  Gathering but it's not magic that Primal  Outpost looks most similar to when it's  later played on the Airship instead  there's actually another popular board  game that Primal Outpost seems to be  both paying homage to and criticizing a  setup for Primal Outpost is title based  and the objective of the game is to gain  and trade resources while watching the  movie it's easy to see that strange  world is evoking Settlers of Catan one  of the most popular strategy board games  of all time while the collectible card  game elements and some of the in-game  rules stray from what players can do in  Catan Primal Outpost definitely feels  like a commentary on that game in  particular much of this critical  commentary comes from Ethan that's  Jaeger and Searcher argue about how to  fight in the game Ethan gets  increasingly frustrated He suggests that  the point of Primal Outpost is to use  your resources to Build a Better World  which is the exact opposite of the  colony this fantasy of Catan and games  of its ilk  by the Final Act has become increasingly  obvious that President Mal and Searcher  aren't on the right as Ethan bonds would  Splat and finds ore in the beauty of  this new world they've discovered  everything about the mission to save the  Pando plant starts to make him uneasy  towards the end of the movie It's  revealed to search her and Ethan exactly  how wrong they are solidifying one of  the main themes of strange world in the  process after a classic fathers and  fight Ethan runs off the Airship and  Searcher follows eventually the two  discover themselves in a location Jaeger  was trying to reach all along on the  other side of the mountains it's here  that they discover their Planet as a  literal living being sadly the being  that avalonia sits atop is dying and  specifically it is being killed by the  avalonians harvesting the Pando plans  for their energy this twist turns a  story that was already about the  environment into a full-on metaphor for  the climate change crisis facing our  planet Strange World literally makes  this planet a living breathing creature  in order to communicate the idea to his  younger audience that the planet is  alive and can be harmed in the end  strange world is about learning to fix  our mistakes but also about making  sacrifices in order to adjust to a new  healthier world  after the story wraps up the audience is  transported to one year later in a Flash  Forward a voiceover from Ethan reveals  what happens to avalonia following the  events of strange world in the epilogue  Ethan talks about how the last year has  been incredibly difficult but that  everyone has proven just how resilient  they are considering the fact that  strange world is being released at the  tail end of the covid-19 pandemic is  hard not to think that Ethan's sentiment  might have a deeper meaning strange  world is far from a throwaway animation  and instead contains a crucial subtext  about climate change that mainly adults  and older teens will pick up on but  beyond that Ethan's talk of resilience  appears to reference a pandemic in  particular this moment serves as a  rallying cry for all the viewers who  fought through a hard year but must  continue doing the work to enact change  ultimately this call to action as the  overarching theme of strange world with  a movie asking viewers to care for the  planet before it's too late  [Music]
 

